Description: AstraOS Xfce desktop configuration
 The AstraOS desktop: the Windows-11 style taskbar layout, keyboard shortcuts,
 window-manager and desktop settings, the skeleton home directory that seeds
 every new account (panel, neon terminal, compositor profile), the AstraOS
 application launchers, and the opt-in picom animation profile.
 .
 The desktop is CONFIGURED Xfce, not a replacement for it. AstraOS does not
 ship a custom shell, window manager or session manager (plan §7). Configuration is
 applied through /etc/skel, the mechanism Xfce uses for a new account's defaults, so
 the interface stays user-configurable and upgradable with the upstream packages.
 .
 The defaults are deliberately NOT written to /etc/xdg/xfce4/xfconf/xfce-perchannel-xml:
 those paths belong to Debian's Xfce packages, and dpkg refuses to let two packages own
 the same file.
 .
 The window chrome carries a light frame opacity and translucent move/resize
 (the HUD glass look); the heavier fade-on-open animation is opt-in through
 `astra effects on` and ships as /etc/astraos/picom.conf, because the default
 must stay the compositor that renders correctly everywhere.
